<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<!--
  Open Duck Mini v2 — URDF design ledger
  ======================================
  Repaired 2026-08-12 (task_plan_v2.md Task M7, branch A "fix and gate").
  Originally an onshape-to-robot export; it had never validated.

  STATUS AND AUTHORITY
    NOT the source of truth for simulation. The Isaac/PhysX pipeline builds its
    USD from robot_motors.xml (MJCF) via scripts/convert_mjcf_to_usd.py; this
    file is in no training or evaluation code path. It is kept because it is the
    standard interchange format (RViz / MoveIt / Gazebo) and because it is an
    independent cross-check on the MJCF — see CROSS-CHECK below.
    tests/test_urdf_consistency.py fails if the two descriptions drift.

  UNITS AND FRAMES
    Lengths metres, angles radians, mass kilograms (URDF convention).
    Joint <origin> is the child link frame expressed in the parent link frame.
    Joint <axis> is expressed in the CHILD link frame.
    <visual>/<collision>/<inertial> origins are expressed in their own link frame.
    Meshes are authored in metres and referenced with paths RELATIVE to this
    file; every .stl sits in this directory. Mesh scale is 1.0 (no <scale>).

  TOPOLOGY (verified by the urdf skill validator)
    root link      trunk_assembly   (carries real mass; there is no massless
                                     wrapper link, and there never was one here
                                     — the MJCF's `base` wrapper was the anomaly
                                     and was merged away on 2026-08-11, PLANT-1)
    21 links, 20 joints, 16 movable (revolute) + 4 fixed frame joints
    total mass     2.657 kg

  FRAME-ONLY LINKS
    trunk, left_foot, right_foot, head carry NO <inertial> and no geometry.
    They are pure kinematic frames attached by fixed joints. Their previous
    zero-diagonal inertia tensors were invalid URDF (a zero inertia diagonal is
    not a legal rigid body) and are removed rather than replaced with an
    invented epsilon. The equivalent MJCF markers use mass=1e-09; PhysX
    substitutes 4.0e-12 for them at load, which is benign (known_issues PLANT-1b).

  REPAIRS APPLIED 2026-08-12
    1. 266 mesh references were `package:///<name>.stl` — a package:// URI with
       an EMPTY package name, unresolvable by every standard consumer. Rewritten
       to plain relative paths. All 47 distinct meshes verified present on disk.
    2. Removed the invalid zero-inertia <inertial> from the four frame links.

  KNOWN, DELIBERATE NON-STANDARD ELEMENTS (validator reports these as warnings)
    <mujoco><compiler fusestatic="false"/></mujoco> and the per-joint
    <joint_properties> blocks are MuJoCo compiler hints carried over from the
    upstream export. They are ignored by URDF consumers. Left in place on
    purpose; do not "fix" them.

  ASSUMPTIONS NOT INDEPENDENTLY VERIFIED
    Link inertia tensors and joint limits are inherited from the upstream
    Onshape export and were NOT re-derived here. The mass model is being rebuilt
    in task_plan_v2.md Phase M; when it lands, this file's inertials are stale
    until regenerated. This ledger does not certify them.
-->
<robot name="onshape">
    <mujoco>
        <compiler fusestatic="false"/>
    </mujoco>
    <link name="trunk_assembly">
